{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "06FW", "placeholders": {"FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001": "}", "FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001": "\\footnote{", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$x \\in |\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X}_{\\text{ft-pts}}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-point-finite-type}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-finite-type-point}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4c3183cd2387ca73b9e798aa458ba9ba849cb1da68c37cc70bb1903ba329bd25", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a283bdae598b2fe60fa7c9ddf0eaaf88a3d2e65328b4380481809d46e84d6fe1", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an algebraic stack. We say a point <MATH_0002>\nis a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>finite type point<TEXTITCLOSE_0001><FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001>This is a\nslight abuse of language as it would perhaps be more correct to say\n``locally finite type point''.<FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001> if the equivalent conditions of\nLemma <REF_0001>\nare satisfied. We denote <MATH_0003>\nthe set of finite type points of <MATH_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2c4e9a02c6961f62f0ef3c2317c9409e973a5c0827cf613783c7f5df382370bf", "unit_id": "tag:06FY:statement"}
